# Indeed collector — environment template (ADR-027, ADR-028)
#
# Copy to .env in this directory and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file
# is not. Consumed by systemd's EnvironmentFile= (argos-indeed-collect.service),
# not by argos-career's own .env — this runs as a fully separate process.

# --- argos-career's ingest endpoint -------------------------------------------
# Atlas's Tailscale address and port — the same one Hermes reaches, from the
# same machine this script runs on (Atlas's host, not inside any container).
ARGOS_API_URL=http://100.x.x.x:3000

# Indeed-only credential. Its matching server-side value is
# INGEST_INDEED_API_KEY; it cannot call scoring, Telegram or other sources.
ARGOS_INGEST_API_KEY=

# --- Search parameters (all optional, shown with their defaults) -------------
# SEARCH_TERMS is a comma-separated list, run in one container invocation
# and merged (deduplicated by jobspy's row id) before a single ingest POST
# (ADR-060). Defaults to collect.py's DEFAULT_SEARCH_TERMS — five terms
# measured with `npm run probe:indeed` against a real dry-run scrape, each
# one clearing "real volume that survives the pre-filter and lands in the
# target metro area or remote," the same bar criteria.yaml's own Gupy query
# comments use. See collect.py's own comment for the per-term numbers and
# the two candidates ("estagio dados", "estagio programador") that were
# measured and deliberately left out.
# SEARCH_TERMS=estagio ti,estagio desenvolvimento,estagio suporte,estagio seguranca da informacao,estagio infraestrutura
#
# SEARCH_TERM (singular) still works as a one-term override for
# compatibility — set it instead of SEARCH_TERMS to run only one search.
# SEARCH_TERM=estagio ti
# LOCATION=Rio de Janeiro, Brazil
# COUNTRY_INDEED=Brazil
# RESULTS_WANTED=50
